Always use TypeScript strict mode.

Prefer Server Components; only use "use client" where interactivity is required.

Keep Prisma schema comments explaining DBMS design decisions (this is a coursework project).

Never invent env vars silently — add new ones to .env.example and mention them in chat.

After generating a feature, briefly list:
- what you built
- what still needs manual setup (database provisioning, API keys, etc.)